  "evidence": "SwissWatchExpo 60399 original specimen. All 12 original gallery files inspected 17 November 2026. Movement 8 reviewed at 1200px from original 2530px file: visible 3135 bridge stamp and partly covered THIRTY-ONE rotor inscription. Dealer 31-jewel count is attribution rather than fully unobscured numeric inscription. Case engraving 7 visibly 116600. Black Sea-Dweller dial, date without loupe, elapsed-time bezel, valve-side case view and steel-coloured Oyster/flip-lock visible. Dealer attributes 40mm steel case, ceramic bezel and sapphire crystal; these remain attributions. No specimen year supplied or inferred from random-style serial. Dial depth text does not establish current pressure resistance. No transfer to earlier 16600 or later 126600. No transfer to neighbouring references or other unopened specimens; original fitment, service status, full chronology and user-watch authenticity are not independently established. Existing photographs remain separate specimens. Overall execution/period research remains incomplete.",
